- How would you adapt to allow at most k blocks or variable block values (e.g., using different per-block metrics)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a three-dimensional DP that models constrained path planning with a binary obstacle grid and a budget of unblocks. Requires careful state definition, transitions, and path reconstruction. 

## Key Concepts
- DP with an extra dimension for unblocks (t)
- Handling blocked vs unblocked cells in transitions
- Path reconstruction from 3D DP table
- Time/space trade-offs and rolling optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPath(grid, blocked, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: m}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG)));
  if (!blocked[0][0]) dp[0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  else if (k > 0) dp[0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        const val = grid[i][j];
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t-1] + val);
        }
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t-1] + val);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n-1][m-1][0];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you recover the actual path from the 3D DP and handle ties?
- What optimizations would you apply for large grids or memory constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a new DP angle: subarray-level min as value, exact k non-overlapping blocks, with clear reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exact block count
- Precomputation of subarray minima
- Backtracking to obtain endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Assumes A is 1-indexed, n = A.length-1, k given
function maxSumMinSubarrays(A, n, k) {
  const M = Array.from({length: n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));
  for (let l=1; l<=n; l++) {
    let m = A[l];
    for (let r=l; r<=n; r++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[r]);
      M[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const opt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      for (let l=1; l<=i; l++) {
        const cand = dp[l-1][t-1] + M[l][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; opt[i][t] = l; }
      }
    }
  }
  // backtrack for endpoints
  let i = n, t = k, blocks = [];
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = opt[i][t];
    blocks.push([l, i]);
    i = l-1; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```
